Protocol knowledge attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No third-party code is included in this repository. The BedJet BLE protocol is
undocumented by its manufacturer, and this project's understanding of it builds on
prior reverse-engineering work by others. That work deserves credit even where no
code was taken from it.

  * The ESPHome project — esphome/components/bedjet
    https://github.com/esphome/esphome
    The most complete public description of the BedJet V3 status packet, the
    partial-packet/follow-up-read behaviour, notification semantics, and the
    fan-step and temperature encodings.
    ESPHome's C++ sources are GPLv3. No ESPHome code is used, copied, or ported
    here; it was read as technical evidence only. See docs/decisions/ADR-0003.

  * pjt0620 — Home-Assistant-Bedjet (GPL-3.0)
    https://github.com/pjt0620/Home-Assistant-Bedjet
    Independent corroboration of the GATT layout, and the command opcode and mode
    value tables. No code used or ported.

  * markus1189 — bedjet-re (no licence granted)
    https://github.com/markus1189/bedjet-re
    Documentation of the Biorhythm sequence format and the fragment-transfer
    protocol on characteristic 2005. Referenced as documentation only; nothing
    from it is reproduced here.

  * asheliahut/ha-bedjet, robert-friedland/ha-bedjet, blueharford/ha-bedjet-v3 (MIT)
    Home Assistant custom integrations consulted during the ecosystem survey.

Per-field provenance and confidence for everything this project believes about the
protocol is recorded in docs/protocol/PROTOCOL.md.
